{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"Attention-based NMT alignments are substantially worse than conventional alignment models, with an AER of 54 versus 30 for Chinese-to-English as reported in a prior work.","source_span":"there is a substantial gap in quality between the alignments derived by this attention based NMT and conventional alignment models (54 VS 30 in terms of AER for Chinese-to-English as reported in BIBREF6 )"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"The paper proposes a Supervised Attention based NMT (SA-NMT) model.","source_span":"we propose a Supervised Attention based NMT (SA-NMT) model"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"SA-NMT first runs off-the-shelf aligners such as GIZA++ or fast_align to obtain alignments of the bilingual training corpus in advance.","source_span":"we first run off-the-shelf aligners (GIZA++ BIBREF3 or fast_align BIBREF4 etc.) to obtain the alignment of the bilingual training corpus in advance"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"Experiments were conducted on two Chinese-to-English translation tasks.","source_span":"Experiments on two Chinese-to-English translation tasks show that the super- vised attention mechanism yields better alignments"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"NMT uses two bidirectional recurrent neural networks to encode the source sentence into a sequence of vectors.","source_span":"it uses two bidirectional recurrent neural networks to encode INLINEFORM4 into a sequence of vectors"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"The RNN hidden state activation function used in NMT is a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU).","source_span":"is defined by an activation function, i.e. a Gated Recurrent Unit BIBREF8"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","statement":"SA-NMT implements the supervision of attention as a regularization term in the joint training objective.","source_span":"it implements the supervision of attention as a regularization in the joint training objective (§3.2)"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0079","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What AER scores were reported when comparing attention-based NMT alignments to conventional alignment models on Chinese-to-English translation?","answer":"Attention-based NMT had an AER of 54, compared to 30 for conventional alignment models, on Chinese-to-English translation."}
